Notebook[{
Cell["PadicRational", "ObjectName",ExpressionUUID->"9852db88-32ff-4812-a496-1a3fad7e16b3"],

Cell["\<\
PadicRational[m,p,e,n,k] stores an exact rational with valuation e and n \
normalized unit digits packed into the nonnegative integer m; the highest k \
digits repeat toward the left. For k=0 its value is m p^e. Normal[s] returns \
its exact rational value. Prefer Padic to construct valid canonical objects; \
direct construction does not validate the fields.\
\>", "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"1859cd42-b357-4a89-90bf-ffbd229b0c37"],

Cell["\<\
Prefer Padic[r,p] to construct valid canonical objects. Direct application of \
this representation head does not validate the fields.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"2c8b3c02-206c-48be-87ec-bc550681a754"],

Cell["\<\
The significand packs n normalized unit digits. Its highest k digits repeat \
toward the left; the remaining n-k digits form the finite suffix. Normal \
computes the represented rational exactly.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"9ce36e71-3a76-4ff7-9712-485787c1ddc5"],

Cell["\<\
Arithmetic returns canonical exact values, selecting the smaller base when \
exact operands use different bases. Use Padic[s,p] for an explicit exact base \
conversion.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"9ec38f1c-835a-4515-97a0-d975e9fe31ce"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Needs", "[", "\"\<PadicNumbers`\>\"", 
  "]"}]], "ExampleInitialization",ExpressionUUID->"834f4c12-970c-426a-bd64-\
4d806f337c31"],

